      "finished": true,
      "stop_reason": "finish",
      "summary": "Resolved ticket #39 (Gita Garcia, Acme Logistics). The \"stranger\" (Jonas Mendes, jonas.mendes@brightwave.health) was a cross-tenant data leak, not a real membership. Root cause: RLS was disabled on the `project_members` table (the only tenant-scoped table without a tenant_isolation policy), so the member-list v2 endpoint (/app/tenants/{id}/member-list) returned project-members rows from ALL tenants (Acme, Brightwave, Copperleaf) to any tenant. Fixed by enabling RLS on project_members via POST /app/admin/rls/project_members with the standard tenant_isolation policy (tenant_column=tenant_id). Verified: /app/tenants/2/member-list now returns only acmelogistics.com members. Filed high-severity security notification id 1001 affecting tenants 2, 3, 4. No actual cross-tenant membership data existed; it was a read/isolation bug only.",
